@* Exercise 029 — ClientAuthIsNotEnforcement (web-blazor).
   Goal:   Hide the Approve button from anyone who is not an approver. This is
           the UI-trimming half of the exercise; the enforcement half lives in
           Ex029_PayrollService.TryApprove, which a test calls directly,
           bypassing this component entirely, to prove that hiding the button
           is not enough on its own. Implement ApproverRole so the
           AuthorizeView below requires the right role name.
   Drills: UI trimming is not authorization, server-side enforcement.
   Passes: use facts - an approver-role state renders the Approve button; any
                       other state (including anonymous) does not. *@

<AuthorizeView Roles="@ApproverRole()">
    <Authorized>
        <button id="approve">Approve</button>
    </Authorized>
</AuthorizeView>

@code {
    // Shape A: the AuthorizeView above evaluates this member as its Roles
